Description: Keep GPU loader options separate from the libLLVM global registry
 Peios links every LLVM tool against the shared libLLVM, which makes
 llvm-gpu-loader's options collide with libLLVM's at startup (see Bug below).
Author: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Origin: vendor, tool-local OptTable modelled on upstream llvm-strings
Forwarded: no
Bug: Linking against the complete libLLVM registers ThinLTO's threads option and
 collides with llvm-gpu-loader's threads alias before main. Preserve loader aliases
 and ConsumeAfter arguments with a private option table; keep dynamic LLVM linkage.
Validation: Exact Debian reference one-tool compile/link; 55 parser cases; CLI lit
 regression; all 115 manual probes and complete 116-page manual generation pass.

